    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0330" n="318" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg318"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0010/33: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Huddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bern</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-28"
                            >February 28, 1942</date>.<lb/>[Received February 28—8:40
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>808. American interests—Germany. Department’s 485, February 19th.<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d250-f1"/> Swiss Minister, Berlin,<anchor n="29a" xml:id="d250-f2"/>
                    telegraphs February 24th following: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Ministry Foreign Affairs informs me officially that exchange German
                            group in South American countries which broke diplomatic relations after
                            conference Rio de Janeiro<anchor n="29b" xml:id="d250-f3"/> will not
                            take place via United States.</p>
                        <p>German diplomats in Brazil will be exchanged directly against Brazilian
                            group. All others will be assembled at Buenos Aires and transported from
                            there aboard Argentine vessel to Lisbon. Arrangements to this end have
                            been made with Argentinian and Brazilian Governments. Please inform
                            State Department and Governments of Peru and Uruguay. Colombian
                            diplomats in Germany will join perhaps above mentioned group as they
                            prefer themselves to return with Brazilian group to avoid detour by
                            United States. I would like to receive from State Department indications
                            still lacking regarding exchange, the ship and its course.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Swiss Foreign Office adds as exchange arrangements of personnel formerly
                    accredited other American Republics have been handled by Department it would
                    appreciate Governments Peru, Uruguay and Colombia being informed foregoing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huddle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
